Fold-API approval closed out (2026-09-16). sofar-cloud logged it as enterprise D4 (commit 459d8b4) with our conditions as their standing rule; their task 1.2 is a normal dependency now and v2-sync-team carries a pointer to where the ceiling's replacement lives.
Three consumer requirements relayed to r1-fixes (builder) and rust-core (mirror), to go into the contract Decision:
(1) the snapshot's version (schema hash + engine version) is a READABLE public field, not only an internal check — ingest logs and alerts on mismatch-driven refolds, otherwise a post-upgrade refold storm surfaces as an unexplained latency spike;
(2) the parity and order-independence tests get STABLE names or ids, treated as public API, because procurement answers cite them by name — renaming one needs its own Decision;
(3) when the release carrying the API ships, cloud is told the VERSION, since ingest cannot ship against an engine that predates the contract.
Remaining open number on cloud's side, not ours: repos per org (their range is per org, ours per repo) — the founder pins it.

